# Deferred: Settings Preferences expansion

**Status:** Parked. Revisit later. Do not implement the full Preferences IA unless the user asks.

## Principle

**Preferences = personalize surface and catalog.** Users can hide, show, order, and extend optional attributes. They cannot redefine that an item has a category, that colors attach via item↔color, or that wardrobes are the sharing boundary.

## Current baseline (started)

- Settings → Attribute Preferences (`AttributePreferencesView`) with Colors, Seasons, Categories (+ indented subcategory toggles).
- Draft toggles + toolbar **Save**; Back with unsaved edits → discard alert.
- `isVisible` on Color, Season, Category, Subcategory; pickers filter visible catalog rows.
- Developer tools live under Settings → Developer → Developer Settings (separate from Preferences).

## When revisiting — ship under Settings → **Preferences**

Suggested layout:

```
Preferences
  • Attribute Preferences
  • Display Preferences
  • Profile & Sharing
  • Units
```

Add a **Preferences** section in `SettingsView` and move Attribute Preferences under it when expanding.

---

### 1. Attribute Preferences *(partially done)*

**Done:** Colors, Seasons, Categories (+ subcategory visibility cascade when parent hidden).

**Still to add (from earlier table):**

| Include | Why |
|---|---|
| Categories you use (show/hide *your* list in pickers) | Partially done via `isVisible`; confirm UX copy/footer |
| Optional attributes on/off for *your* add flows | e.g. weather, weight, price, links, location, notes — fewer fields when adding |
| Default units / preferred size scales | Prefer Alpha vs Numeric where both exist |

| Keep out / elsewhere | Why |
|---|---|
| Creating custom colors/seasons/tags | In-flow on item edit (or light “Manage catalog” later) |
| Rewiring category → subcategory → size | Core model; extend lists, not the graph |
| Changing which attribute *types* exist on Item | Product capability (`AppCapabilities`), not user preference |

**Footer idea:** “Hide attributes you don’t use. Your items keep any values already set.”

