### 2. Display Preferences

**How *you* see the app on this device (mostly local).** Add when there are 2+ real toggles.

| Include | Why |
|---|---|
| Grid density / columns | Personal viewing |
| Sort defaults (newest, name, brand…) | Personal viewing |
| Default closet vs wishlist landing | Personal |
| Calendar week start / default view | Personal |
| Show/hide empty attribute rows on *your* item detail | Clutter control |
| Compact vs full attribute labels | Personal |

| Keep out | Why |
|---|---|
| What *others* see on your profile | Profile & Sharing, not Display |
| Feature flags (Fitting tab, sync) | Product tier / `AppCapabilities` |

---

### 3. Profile & Sharing Preferences *(separate from Display)*

**What of *your* wardrobe/social surface is visible to others.**

| Include | Why |
|---|---|
| Default wardrobe visibility (public / friends / private) | Already have per-wardrobe visibility |
| Which wardrobes appear on profile | Sharing boundary already modeled |
| Profile fields shown to others | Username always; optional: style tags, follower counts, bio |
| Show likes / social row on your public items | Engagement surface |
| Who can suggest outfits / Redress you | Social preference if added |

| Keep out | Why |
|---|---|
| Edit avatar / username / style tags *content* | **Edit Profile**; Settings can link, don’t duplicate the editor |
| Friend request management | Notifications / social inbox |

---

### 4. Units & measurements *(small)*

| Include | Notes |
|---|---|
| Weight unit (kg / lbs) | Already `@AppStorage`; move **value** toward profile/body, **unit** here |
| Currency for price display | If prices are localized later |
| Measurement system for sizes | Display preference only |

Can live under Preferences as its own row, or nested under Attribute Preferences if it stays tiny.

---

## Stay true to Redress (do not expose as preferences)

- Removing the category concept or making items category-free by setting
- Remapping how sizes belong to categories
- Turning off wardrobes, sync semantics, or item–outfit–event relationships
- Renaming system attribute *types* (Color vs Season)—only hide instances

**OK if framed carefully:** “Manage my categories” = add/hide *their* rows; “Show price on profile item cards” = display/sharing, not changing that price is an item attribute.

## Out of Preferences (other Settings sections)

- **Account** — email, sign out, delete
- **Notifications** — push prefs (later)
- **Support / Legal** — feedback, privacy, terms
- **Developer** — already gated under Developer Settings

## Practical first cut (when un-parking)

1. Add Preferences section; keep Attribute Preferences as first child.
2. Profile & Sharing when wardrobe/profile visibility UX is ready.
3. Units — weight unit only.
4. Display Preferences only once ≥2 real toggles exist.
